\section{Evaluation Seed Robustness}
\label{sec:appendix_eval_seed}

To verify that our conclusions are not artifacts of a particular evaluation seed, we re-evaluate key model configurations under multiple evaluation seeds (200 episodes each). Table~\ref{tab:eval_seed_robustness} reports aggregate CAR and TSR across all tested seeds.

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Eval-seed robustness: aggregate CAR and TSR (\%) across evaluation seeds (200 episodes each). Dashes indicate untested seeds. CAR ranges overlap across all three conditions, confirming that SDF redundancy is not an eval-seed artifact.}
\label{tab:eval_seed_robustness}
\vspace{2pt}
\footnotesize
\begin{tabular}{llccccccl}
\toprule
& & \multicolumn{6}{c}{Evaluation seed} & \\
\cmidrule(lr){3-8}
Condition & & 0 & 7 & 42 & 99 & 123 & 256 & Mean$\pm$Std \\
\midrule
\multirow{2}{*}{LoRA s0}
  & CAR & 53.0 & 56.5 & 56.5 & 57.5 & 53.0 & --- & 55.3$\pm$2.1 \\
  & TSR & 55.5 & 51.5 & 46.0 & 52.0 & 50.5 & --- & 51.1$\pm$3.4 \\
\midrule
\multirow{2}{*}{SDF $\lambda{=}0.01$ s0}
  & CAR & 52.5 & 57.0 & --- & 57.0 & --- & --- & 55.5$\pm$2.6 \\
  & TSR & 48.5 & 52.5 & --- & 46.5 & --- & --- & 49.2$\pm$3.1 \\
\midrule
\multirow{2}{*}{SDF $\lambda{=}0.1$ s0}
  & CAR & --- & 58.0 & 59.0 & --- & 58.5 & 57.0 & 58.1$\pm$0.9 \\
  & TSR & --- & 47.0 & 52.5 & --- & 53.5 & 48.0 & 50.3$\pm$3.2 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

LoRA s0 CAR ranges from 53.0\% to 57.5\% across five evaluation seeds (std\,=\,2.1\,pp), consistent with binomial sampling noise at $n{=}50$ episodes per task. SDF $\lambda{=}0.01$ s0 produces near-identical mean CAR (55.5\% vs.\ 55.3\%), confirming that the null result holds across eval conditions. SDF $\lambda{=}0.1$ s0 shows a slightly higher mean (58.1\%), but the ranges overlap with LoRA-only, and the difference (2.8\,pp, ${<}$1.3$\sigma$) remains non-significant. The per-task CAR ordering (chocolate\_pudding highest, bbq\_sauce lowest) is preserved across all seeds and conditions, reinforcing the demonstration-driven avoidance hypothesis.

